{
  "id": "039",
  "title": "The Fourteenth Loop",
  "subtitle": "\"Every week is the same week. I have lived it thirteen times. On the fourteenth loop I stop trying to save everyone and start trying to figure out what the System wants.\"",
  "penName": "Eliot Mahr",
  "genre": "regressionTimeloop",
  "hook": "The week begins on Monday. It ends on Sunday at 11:47 PM. On the first loop I tried to save my sister. On the second I tried to save the kids in the school bus. On the third I tried to save the town. By the thirteenth loop I had watched everyone I know die in every combination of ways. On the fourteenth loop I sat down at my kitchen table on Monday at 6:14 AM and I did not go outside. I read the System notification that had always been there and I had always ignored.",
